B.afj=s(["2 WARS IN THE EAST\n\nKEY POINTS FOR THIS LESSON:\n\u2022 explain the causes, course, and results of Poland\u2019s wars with Muscovy in the 17th century,\n\u2022 discuss the Khmelnytsky Uprising,\n\u2022 describe changes to Poland\u2019s eastern border.\n\n1598\u20131613 \u2014 Time of Troubles in the Muscovite state\n1610 \u2014 Battle of Klushino and capture of Moscow by Polish forces\n1648 \u2014 outbreak of the Khmelnytsky Uprising\n\n\u25a0 TIME OF TROUBLES\nAt the turn of the 16th and 17th centuries the Muscovite state fell into deep crisis. The last Rurik ruler, Tsar Fyodor I, died. Boris Godunov took the throne.\n\n\u25a0 TIME OF THE DIMITRIADS\nInternal unrest and famine spread. A pretender appeared \u2014 False Dmitry I.","WARS IN THE EAST\n\n\u25a0 WAR OF THE COMMONWEALTH WITH MUSCOVY\nIn 1604 new uprisings broke out in Russia. Polish magnates supported False Dmitry I. After his death Vasili Shuysky became tsar.\n\nThe Dimitriads were private military expeditions of Polish nobles into Muscovy.\n\nThe Battle of Klushino in 1610 ended in a Polish victory led by Hetman Stanis\u0142aw \u017b\xf3\u0142kiewski."],t.s)
B.Xr=new A.ek("Wars in the East",B.afj,4)
B.ac5=s(["FROM POWER TO THE COMMONWEALTH\u2019S DEFEATS\n\nWARS WITH MUSCOVY IN THE FIRST HALF OF THE 17TH CENTURY\n\n\u25a0 WAR FOR SMOLE\u0143SK\nIn 1632 Tsar Michael Romanov began a war to retake Smolensk. The siege lasted nearly two years.\n\nHISTORICAL FIGURE\nW\u0141ADYS\u0141AW IV VASA (1595\u20131648)\nKing of Poland and Grand Duke of Lithuania. Led wars against Muscovy and the Ottoman Empire.","WARS IN THE EAST\n\n\u25a0 COSSACKS\nIn the 16th and 17th centuries Cossacks settled on the Wild Fields in the south-east of the Commonwealth.\n\nReasons for Cossack revolts:\n\u2022 social and economic oppression,\n\u2022 limits on the Cossack register,\n\u2022 religious differences \u2014 Orthodoxy and the Union of Brest,\n\u2022 ethnic distinctiveness.\n\nZaporizhzhia \u2014 Cossack centre on the Dnieper."],t.s)
B.Xp=new A.ek("War for Smolensk",B.ac5,0)
B.aa0=s(["FROM POWER TO THE COMMONWEALTH\u2019S DEFEATS\n\n\u25a0 OUTBREAK OF THE KHMELNYTSKY UPRISING\nIn 1648 a Cossack rebellion led by Bohdan Khmelnytsky erupted in Ukraine.\n\nHISTORICAL FIGURE\nBOHDAN KHMELNYTSKY (1595\u20131657)\nCossack hetman and leader of the uprising.\n\nBattles:\n\u2022 Yellow Waters (2\u20136 May 1648),\n\u2022 Korsun (26 May 1648),\n\u2022 Pyliavtsi (13\u201314 September 1648).","WARS IN THE EAST\n\nKHMELNYTSKY UPRISING AND THE POLISH-RUSSIAN WAR\n\n1. Define the territorial scope of Khmelnytsky\u2019s uprising.\n2. List areas the Commonwealth lost to Muscovy in 1667.\n\nThe Battle of Zboriv ended without a clear victor but enabled a treaty with the Cossacks."],t.s)
B.Xn=new A.ek("Outbreak of the Khmelnytsky Uprising",B.aa0,5)
B.a1o=s(["FROM POWER TO THE COMMONWEALTH\u2019S DEFEATS\n\nSOURCE TEXT\nBATTLE OF BERESTECHKO\nJoachim Jerlicz described the battle of Berestechko in 1651 in his memoir.\n\n\u25a0 FROM ZBARAZH TO BATOHO\nAfter W\u0142adys\u0142aw IV died, John Casimir Vasa became king. Jeremi Wi\u015bniowiecki won several victories against rebels."],t.s)
B.Xq=new A.ek("From Zbarazh to Batoh",B.a1o,2)
B.acK=s(["WARS IN THE EAST\n\n\u25a0 MOSCOW IN THE COSSACK CONFLICT\nKhmelnytsky turned to Moscow for help. In 1654 the Pereyaslav Agreement recognised the tsar\u2019s sovereignty.\n\n1658 \u2014 Union of Hadiach: a project of a three-nation Commonwealth.\n1667 \u2014 Truce of Andrusovo: Ukraine divided along the Dnieper.\n1686 \u2014 Eternal Peace with Muscovy."],t.s)
B.Xx=new A.ek("Moscow in the Cossack conflict",B.acK,9)
B.a1K=s(["3 WARS WITH SWEDEN AND THE COMMONWEALTH CRISIS\n\nKEY POINTS:\n\u2022 causes and results of wars with Sweden,\n\u2022 crisis of the state in the 17th century,\n\u2022 changes on the northern border.\n\n1605 \u2014 Battle of Kircholm\n1655\u20131660 \u2014 Swedish Deluge\n\n\u25a0 WAR FOR LIVONIA\nSigismund III sought to regain Livonia. Jan Karol Chodkiewicz won at Bia\u0142y Kamie\u0144 (1604) and Kircholm (1605).","POLISH-SWEDISH CONFLICT IN THE FIRST HALF OF THE 17TH CENTURY\n\nWAR FOR THE VISTULA ESTUARY\nGustav II Adolf attacked Livonia in 1621. The naval Battle of Oliwa (1627) was won by the Polish fleet.\n\nINFOGRAPHIC \u2014 BATTLE OF OLIWA\nOn 28 November 1627 Admiral Arend Dickmann\u2019s fleet defeated the Swedes at the mouth of the Vistula."],t.s)
B.Xj=new A.ek("Wars with Sweden and the Commonwealth crisis",B.a1K,3)
B.a5l=s(["5.2 Ventilation and gas exchange\n\nImportant in this lesson!\n\u2022 explain lung ventilation,\n\u2022 describe gas exchange in lungs and tissues,\n\u2022 outline transport of respiratory gases and the role of haemoglobin.\n\nHumans breathe dozens of times per minute. Inhalation and exhalation are driven by the rib muscles and diaphragm.","5.2 Ventilation and gas exchange\n\nWhat is gas exchange?\nSupplying oxygen to cells and removing carbon dioxide \u2014 by diffusion in the lungs (external) and tissues (internal).\n\nInhaled air: nitrogen 78%, oxygen 21%, CO\u2082 0.03%.\nExhaled air: oxygen 16%, CO\u2082 4.5%."],t.s)
B.Xi=new A.ek("Ventilation and gas exchange",B.a5l,2)
B.a7F=s(["5.3 Disorders of the respiratory system\n\nImportant in this lesson!\n\u2022 impact of air pollution on health,\n\u2022 prevention of respiratory diseases.\n\nAir pollutants include nitrogen oxides, sulphur oxides, benzopyrene, and particulate matter PM10 and PM2.5.\n\nMain sources in Poland: home stoves, transport, power plants, industry.","5.3 Disorders of the respiratory system\n\nWhat is smog?\nAir pollution combined with fog or water vapour.\n\nCarbon monoxide \u2014 the invisible killer\nCO binds to haemoglobin more strongly than oxygen.\n\nWhy is smoking harmful?\nTobacco smoke contains nicotine, CO, tar, cadmium, and benzopyrene.","Diseases worth knowing\nRespiratory diseases\n\nRhinitis \u2014 inflammation of the nasal mucosa.\nCommon cold vs flu \u2014 flu starts suddenly with fever above 39\xb0C.\nTonsillitis \u2014 bacterial, spread by droplets.\nPulmonary tuberculosis \u2014 caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis.\nLung cancer \u2014 main risk factor: smoking."],t.s)
B.Xm=new A.ek("Respiratory system disorders",B.a7F,9)
B.aeg=s(["6.3 Lymphatic system\n\nImportant in this lesson!\n\u2022 structure and functions of the lymphatic system,\n\u2022 role of lymph,\n\u2022 lymphatic organs.\n\nElements: bone marrow, thymus, lymph nodes, spleen, tonsils, and lymphatic vessels.\n\nLymph forms from tissue fluid and returns proteins and immune cells to the bloodstream."],t.s)
B.Xk=new A.ek("Lymphatic system",B.aeg,0)
B.a8V=s(["6.4 Circulatory system diseases\n\nImportant in this lesson!\n\u2022 link between lifestyle and cardiovascular disease,\n\u2022 diagnostic tests.\n\nLifestyle and heart disease\nHeart and vessel diseases caused 37% of deaths in Poland in 2023.\n\nWhat the circulatory system \u201clikes\u201d:\n\u2022 regular physical activity,\n\u2022 a balanced diet with less saturated fat, sugar, and salt."],t.s)
B.Xs=new A.ek("Circulatory system diseases",B.a8V,0)
